},{"type":"p","children":["Geopolitical events and extreme drought are dampening the appetite for investment Following a start to 2026 marked by the conflict in the Middle East and political uncertainties, demand at Kuhn Group remained subdued overall. The extreme drought in Europe generated lower crop and forage yields. The lower usage of machines in these conditions also weighed on the spare parts business. In the USA, an improvement in the farmers’ willingness to invest has recently been noticeable. Overall, the economic situation for farmers remained strained. While prices for key agricultural commodities have recently increased due to disappointing global harvests, farmers’ operating costs have risen sharply, particularly the prices of fertilisers and diesel. The dairy and livestock sectors proved more resilient but were affected by unfavourable weather conditions, which reduced feed reserves for the coming year. In the first nine months, the division’s order intake remained below the level of prior-year period. Order intake in the third quarter was supported by the earlier launch of the pre-order programmes especially in the USA, which brought forward some demand. Thanks to the higher order book at the beginning of the year, sales reached the previous year’s level. The downturn impacting the market in Brazil caused the local production sites to operate well below capacity. The division continues to work consistently to adapt its cost structures to a challenging market environment."]},{"type":"p","children":["Outlook for 2026 Kuhn Group expects stable sales on a comparable basis. The operating profit margin is expected to be somewhat lower than in 2025."]},{"type":"p","children":["Bucher Municipal"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":[{"type":"b","children":["  "]}]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":2},