howed a mixed performance in the first nine months of 2026. At Bucher Vaslin, customers’ willingness to invest remained subdued due to persistently low wine consumption. Orders at Bucher Unipektin also fell significantly compared with the very high figure of the prior-year period. Bucher Landtechnik’s order intake was on a par with the prior year, while it developed positively at Bucher Automation. Overall, the division’s order intake was below the prior-year period. Sales, on the other hand, rose slightly. The decline in the wine business, which remains under pressure, was offset by positive developments in the other three business units. The consolidation of production sites at Bucher Vaslin, which was initiated in the first half of the year, is well advanced. Preparations for the announced integration of Bucher Automation into the Bucher Hydraulics and Bucher Emhart Glass divisions with effect from the beginning of 2027 are also proceeding as planned. This reorganisation will simplify processes, ease and strengthen the collaboration with internal customers."]},{"type":"p","children":["Outlook for 2026 Bucher Specials anticipates slight sales growth on a comparable basis. The operating profit margin is likely to be lower than in the prior year due to the current business situation at Bucher Vaslin and the restructuring costs."]},{"type":"p","children":["Group outlook 2026"]},{"type":"p","children":["With its strategically chosen approach of local production and proximity to its customers, Bucher Industries is well positioned in the current environment. The Group’s broad set-up also contributes to its stability. For 2026, the Group overall expects slightly lower sales on a comparable basis. The operating profit margin is expected to be below the prior-year level (excluding the profit of CHF 43 million from the sale of a property in 2025)."]},{"type":"p","children":["Expansion of the board of directors"]},{"type":"p","children":["The board of directors will propose Patrick Hess for election at the next annual general meeting on 21 April 2027. Graduated in business administration from the University of Fribourg (Switzerland), he has many years of international management experience in the industry. Patrick Hess is a Swiss national and has held various management positions at Schindler for 25 years. His previous roles have included, amongst others, CFO and CEO of Schindler Aufzüge AG Switzerland as well as head of finance for Schindler in the UK. He has been a member of Schindler’s group management since 2025 and is responsible for the Central, Northern and Eastern European businesses. Patrick Hess will strengthen the board of directors of Bucher Industries with his extensive leadership experience and proven international industrial expertise."]},{"type":"p","children":["Investor day 2027"]},{"type":"p","children":["Bucher Industries is planning an investor day on 1 June 2027. The event will provide insights into the Group’s strategy and the divisions’ priorities, as well as an opportunity to learn more about Bucher Industries’ products and technologies. Further details will be announced at a later date."]},{"type":"p","children":["Contact for investors and financial analysts"]},{"type":"p","children":["Jin Wiederkehr, Investor Relations"]},{"type":"p","children":["T +41 58 750 15 50"]},{"type":"p","children":["ir@bucherindustries.com"]},{"type":"p","children":["Contact for media"]},{"type":"p","children":["Saskia Rusch, Head of Group Communications"]},{"type":"p","children":["T +41 58 750 15 40"]},{"type":"p","children":["media@bucherindustries.com"]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["_________"]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Simply great machines"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Bucher Industries is a global technology group with leading market positions in speciality areas of mechanical and vehicle engineering. The company’s operations include agricultural machinery, municipal vehicles, hydraulic and electronic components as well as electrohydraulic systems, manufacturing equipment for the glass container industry, equipment for processing beverages and automation solutions. The company’s shares are traded on the SIX Swiss Exchange (SIX: BUCN). Further information is available at bucherindustries.com."]},{"type":"p","children":["Additional performance measures: Internally and externally Bucher Industries uses key figures that are not defined by Swiss GAAP FER. The composition and calculation of the individual performance measures are set out here: bucherindustries.com/en/additional-performance-measures."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"disclaimer","children":["Saving the news in databases or any forwarding of the news to third parties in a commercial context or for commercial purposes is only permitted with the prior written consent of EQS Group AG."]}]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"EQS","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"eqs"}]},{"title":"Swiss stocks","args":[{"id":"category","value":"stock"},{"id":"market_country","value":"CH"}]}],"id":"eqs:a687e91d1094b:0","title":"Third quarter 2026: Stabilisation of demand","published":1793077200,"urgency":2,"link":"https://www.eqs-news.com/news/inside-information-ad-hoc-release/third-quarter-2026-stabilisation-of-demand/7b6ffe28-a1cd-41ed-bbb9-f33b3b4bec9e_en","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"SIX:BUCN","logoid":"bucher-n","logo":{"style":"single","logoid":"bucher-n"}}],"storyPath":"/news/eqs:a687e91d1094b:0-third-quarter-2026-stabilisation-of-demand/","read_time":456,"provider":{"id":"eqs","name":"EQS","logo_id":"eqs"}}